{"levels":[{"n":1,"grid":"[Raid Puzzle · teach · Ch1 Village Mat] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 0.47 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 3x\nMY MOVES: hand walk pull\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1o:h5 2o:h7 3o:h7 4o:h7 5o:h7 6o:h7 7o:h5 | home after 1 touch: walk 9% | after 2: walk 12% | if held: pull 48%\nGOAL: score 1 | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Score on your first raid; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 40/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 99/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Teach the raid: pick a defender, Hand Touch him and walk back over the midline. Seven rookies, 3 raids, 1 point needed — the only lesson is that a touch only counts once you are home.","mechanics":["hand touch","walk home"],"optimal":4,"branching":8,"trap":0,"explored":293},{"n":2,"grid":"[Raid Puzzle · teach · Ch1 Village Mat] OPP MAT: T T o o T T T · grip 0.20 · KEY: T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 3x\nMY MOVES: hand walk pull\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1T:h15 2T:h16 3o:h8 4o:h8 5T:h16 6T:h20 7T:h15 | home after 1 touch: walk 23% | after 2: walk 29% | if held: pull 47%\nGOAL: score 2 | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Never get caught; No empty raids\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 40/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 91/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backwa