thers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Chapter boss and the first whole match, kept short: the Village Final as a mini-Blitz of 2x6 game minutes (~17 raids in all) with a half-time swap. Their captain Bholu has a personality you can read: he is greedy — he goes for two touches on 8 raids in 10 and always Dashes home. Aha: his second touch and his Dash are your chances — tackle his next target with the cover, or Ankle his Dash home; on your raids, raid the rookie gaps and Dash past the T's. Win the match.","mechanics":["hand touch","dash home","struggle (pull-away)","ankle hold","thigh hold","cover position","full match"],"optimal":null,"branching":9,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":12,"grid":"[Raid Puzzle · teach · Ch2 District Cup] OPP MAT: T T T T T T T · grip 0.18 · KEY: T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 4x\nMY MOVES: hand toe walk dash pull\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1T:h14/t2 2T:h18/t3 3T:h18/t3 4T:h18/t3 5T:h18/t3 6T:h18/t3 7T:h14/t2 | home after 1 touch: walk 27%, dash 10% | after 2: walk 34%, dash 13% | if held: pull 47%\nGOAL: score 3 | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Never get caught; Win within 3 raids\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 40/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 94/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCO