gine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 37/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 78/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Four Blockers (B) form a wall on the midline — the screen shows it: before you pick the way home the B's link arms across the midline and the Dash gem is drawn against the wall, so a Dash into them (held most of the time, READ) is shown on its gem with a WALLED tag — never a hidden trap. The Dubki ducks under their arms and the T's reach. Aha: dubki under a reach. Score 3 points with at least one Dubki or Toe Touch scoring.","mechanics":["dubki","toe touch","hand touch","blocker wall","thigh-holders"],"optimal":null,"branching":17,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":15,"grid":"[Defend Stand · teach · Ch2 District Cup] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 5 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe walk dash dubki pull | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block hold\nCPU RAIDER \"District sprinter\": s 0.23 · Easy · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash · up to 1 touch\nBLOCK WINDOW: ×1.15 (wider timing for the teaching unit)\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 25/thigh 64; toe: ankle 65/thigh 23 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 28/thigh 49/block 41; dash: ankle 45/thigh 24/block 77 | his touch lands 76% if untackled\nGOAL: stop 3 raids | FAIL: opp scores > 5 | STARS: Win within his first 4 raids; Concede at most 2\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 38/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 90/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Teach the Block: the district sprinter telegraphs his way home — mostly a Dash, sometimes a walk. Against a Dash, let the touch go and form the Block on the midline (its timing window is a little wider in this first lesson, READ); against a walk the Block is weak and the Thigh Hold is the stop. Aha: defend the way home, not the touch — and read WHICH way home before you build the wall. Stop 3 of 5.","mechanics":["block (defensive wall)","ankle hold","thigh hold","return tackle"],"optimal":6,"branching":7,"trap":0,"explored":19896},{"n":16,"grid":"[Match · teach · Ch2 District Cup] OPP MAT: A T A T A T A · grip 0.70 · KEY: A ankle-catcher (Toe/hop/Dubki risky), T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: alternate: 4 raids / 4 defences · start score 8-7 · empty raids 1/0\nMY MOVES: hand toe walk dash pull | DEFENCE: ankle thigh hold\nCPU RAIDER \"District raider\": s 0.44 · Easy · touches hand/toe · home walk · up to 1 touch\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1A:h21/t34 2T:h35/t36 3A:h35/t36 4T:h35/t36 5A:h35/t36 6T:h35/t36 7A:h21/t34 | home after 1 touch: walk 50%, dash 23% | after 2: walk 61%, dash 30% | if held: pull 41%\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 21/thigh 54; toe: ankle 56/thigh 20 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 23/thigh 40 | his touch lands 81% if untackled\nGOAL: win by 1+ | STARS: Exactly one empty raid; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 36/40 (best 2★), a mid-skill player 86/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Teach the empty-raid counter: you lead 8-7, already on 1 empty raid, and their mat is all hard — Ankle-catchers and Thigh-holders in turn, no rookie anywhere, so every touch is a real risk (READ ~20-35% held, the corner A's Hand the lowest) and a caught raid hands them the point and the lead. An empty raid (Walk home without touching) is safe and costs nothing while you lead — but the THIRD empty in a row is Do-or-Die, so you get exactly one free one. Their raider is gentle: your defence wins the points. Aha: one patient empty raid is a weapon, two is a risk — spend the one, then touch with the counter move (Toe on a T, Hand on an A). 4 raids each; finish ahead. The 3-star play is exactly one empty raid.","mechanics":["empty-raid counter","toe touch","hand touch","ankle-catchers","thigh-holders"],"optimal":null,"branching":16,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":17,"grid":"[Do-or-Die Drill · teach · Ch2 District Cup] OPP MAT: A o B B B o A · grip 0.28 · KEY: A ankle-catcher (Toe/hop/Dubki risky), o rookie, B blocker (Dash risky)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 3x · empty raids 2/0\nMY MOVES: hand toe walk dash dubki pull\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1A:h3/t15 2o:h5/t11 3B:h6/t5 4B:h7/t6 5B:h6/t5 6o:h5/t11 7A:h3/t15 | home after 1 touch: walk 15%, dash 33%, dubki 21% | after 2: walk 19%, dash 41%, dubki 27% | if held: pull 47%\nGOAL: score 2, 1x dodWin | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Score 3 points; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 39/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 83/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"One lesson — survive the Do-or-Die: you are on two empty raids, so your FIRST raid must score or your raider is out. Ankle-catchers on the corners, a Blocker wall in the middle: the wall shuts the Dash home and the A's read the Dubki, so the safe way back is a plain walk, and the safe touch is a Hand on a corner A (READ). Win that raid and the trial is yours: score 2 in 3 raids. The greedy 3-point run (a second touch on a free raid after the Do-or-Die) is the star, never the goal. Aha: under Do-or-Die take the surest point, not the biggest.","mechanics":["do-or-die raid","toe touch","hand touch","ankle-catchers","blocker wall"],"optimal":null,"branching":17,"trap":0,"explored":40000},{"n":18,"grid":"[Raid Puzzle · teach · Ch2 District Cup] OPP MAT: o T T o T T o · grip 0.32 · KEY: o rookie, T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 4x\nMY MOVES: hand toe bonus walk dash dubki pull\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1o:h11/t3 2T:h24/t5 3T:h24/t5 4o:h18/t5 5T:h24/t5 6T:h24/t5 7o:h11/t3 bonus:4 | home after 1 touch: walk 28%, dash 12%, dubki 7% | after 2: walk 36%, dash 16%, dubki 9% | if held: pull 46%\nGOAL: score 4, 2x bonus | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Earn 3 bonus points; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 40/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 80/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Teach the bonus line: with 6+ defenders on the mat a hop over the bonus line scores 1 and puts nobody out. Rookie corners make the hop safe. Aha: bonus first — every touch puts a man out and below 6 the bonus line is dead. Earn 2 bonus points and 4 points total in 4 raids.","mechanics":["bonus line","toe touch","hand touch","dubki","thigh-holders"],"optimal":null,"branching":18,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":19,"grid":"[Revival Run · twist · Ch2 District Cup] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 0.39 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o - o o - o (5 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 4 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe walk dash dubki pull | DEFENCE: ankle thigh hold\nCPU RAIDER \"District raider\": s 0.54 · Easy · touches hand/toe · home walk · up to 1 touch\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 20/thigh 50; toe: ankle 52/thigh 18 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 20/thigh 35 | his touch lands 83% if untackled\nGOAL: stop 2 raids | FAIL: opp scores > 3 | STARS: Finish with all 7 on the mat; Win within his first 3 raids\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 35/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 66/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Twist, one lesson — revival: two of your side are already out (5 on the mat). Every point you win brings one back, first out, first back, and a tackle is a point — so each stop is a man returning to the mat, each touch he lands sends another off. Only the two holds you know (no Block): his telegraph shows Hand or Toe, Thigh the Hand, Ankle the Toe, with the cover beside his target. Aha: defence is how you rebuild — two clean stops put all seven back. Stop 2 of his 4 raids and concede no more than 3; finishing with all 7 on the mat is the 3-star rebuild.","mechanics":["revival","ankle hold","thigh hold","cover position"],"optimal":4,"branching":7,"trap":0,"explored":600},{"n":20,"grid":"[Match · spike · Ch2 District Cup] OPP MAT: A o T B T o A · grip 0.70 · KEY: A ankle-catcher (Toe/hop/Dubki risky), o rookie, T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), B blocker (Dash risky)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: alternate: 4 raids / 4 defences · start score 13-13 · empty raids 1/1\nMY MOVES: hand toe bonus walk dash dubki pull | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block hold\nCPU RAIDER \"District star\": s 0.49 · Easy · touches hand/toe/bonus · home walk/dash/dubki · up to 1 touch\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1A:h7/t34 2o:h24/t24 3T:h37/t11 4B:h37/t12 5T:h37/t11 6o:h24/t24 7A:h7/t34 bonus:43 | home after 1 touch: walk 43%, dash 39%, dubki 43% | after 2: walk 53%, dash 48%, dubki 53% | if held: pull 41%\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 20/thigh 52; toe: ankle 54/thigh 19; bonus: ankle 33/thigh 22 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 21/thigh 38/block 27; dash: ankle 34/thigh 18/block 52; dubki: ankle 39/thigh 6/block 9 | his touch lands 82% if untackled\nGOAL: win by 1+ | STARS: Win by 3; No empty raids\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 38/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 84/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Spike built only from chapter 2's verbs: level at 13-13, 4 raids each left. You are on 1 empty raid (one more patient raid is allowed, a second would make the third Do-or-Die), their raider takes one touch or hops the bonus. Ankle-catchers on the corners make your bonus hop a real risk (READ); the rookies in slots 2 and 6 are the safe touches, the T's beside the Blocker want the Toe. Aha: in a one-point game, count the empties — bank one safe Toe point early, then decide whether the bonus is worth its risk. Win by 1.","mechanics":["empty-raid counter","bonus line","toe touch","dubki","block (defensive wall)","ankle-catchers"],"optimal":null,"branching":18,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":21,"grid":"[Ghost Duel · breather · Ch2 District Cup] OPP MAT: o T o o o T o · grip 0.45 · KEY: o rookie, T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 4x\nMY MOVES: hand toe bonus walk dash dubki pull\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1o:h15/t5 2T:h25/t7 3o:h16/t6 4o:h7/t6 5o:h16/t6 6T:h25/t7 7o:h15/t5 bonus:5 | home after 1 touch: walk 25%, dash 12%, dubki 9% | after 2: walk 32%, dash 16%, dubki 13% | if held: pull 44%\nGOAL: beat the ghost's 4 points, 1x bonus | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Earn 2 bonus points; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a com