 telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Teach the defender Rush, and when NOT to use it: the state raider hops for the bonus line on about half his raids and Hand- or Toe-touches on the rest. A corner Rush is the best answer to a hop, but it is the worst answer to a touch — the holds stop touches (READ). So every raid is a read: hop → Rush, Hand → Thigh, Toe → Ankle. Aha: rush the hop, hold the touch. Stop 2 of 4 raids, concede no more than 3.","mechanics":["defender rush","bonus line","ankle hold","thigh hold"],"optimal":4,"branching":10,"trap":0,"explored":1083},{"n":26,"grid":"[Super Challenge · teach · Ch3 State League] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o - - - o - (3 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 4 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nCPU RAIDER \"State raider\": s 0.44 · Medium · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash · up to 2 touches\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 21/thigh 54/rush 32; toe: ankle 56/thigh 20/rush 34 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 23/thigh 40/block 29/rush 17; dash: ankle 36/thigh 19/block 55/ru