d (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Twist, one idea only: state sides scout you. A touch move or way home you used on your PREVIOUS raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and its real % rises (READ row). Rushers sit beside Thigh-holders, so the Kick on a charging R and the Toe on a T are both good touches, and the Dash and the walk both get you home. Aha: the safest move is the one you did not just use — alternate Kick and Toe, Dash and walk. Score 4 in 4 raids with at least one Kick.","mechanics":["defence reads repeats","backward kick","rusher defenders","thigh-holders","toe touch"],"optimal":null,"branching":21,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":28,"grid":"[Super Challenge · teach · Ch3 State League] OPP MAT: o - T A - - o · grip 0.32 · KEY: o rookie, T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), A ankle-catcher (Toe/hop/Dubki risky) · no scouting on this trial (no SCOUTED tags)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 4x\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1o:h11/t3 3T:h18/t12 4A:h11/t18 7o:h4/t10 | home after 1 touch: walk 11%, dash 5%, dubki 12% | after 2: walk 15%, dash 7%, dubki 16% | if held: pull 46%, lunge 45%\nGOAL: 1x allOut | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: All-out within 2 raids; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 38/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 79/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Teach the all-out: four are left — a rookie on each corner and a Thigh-holder beside an Ankle-catcher in the centre. Touch all four out and the all-out is +2 with their whole side coming back — but every point THEY win (a caught raid) revives one of theirs, so a greedy raid that gets caught undoes the work. The centre pair needs two different moves (Toe on the T, Hand on the A, READ) and each extra touch raises the next one's risk. No scouting on this drill. Aha: finish the job in the right order — the hard centre pair first while you are fresh, the corner rookies last, and never let a lone survivor revive them. Inflict the all-out within 4 raids.","mechanics":["all-out","hand touch","toe touch","dubki","thigh-holders","ankle-catchers"],"optimal":null,"branching":11,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":29,"grid":"[Defend Stand · twist · Ch3 State League] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 5 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nCPU RAIDER \"State kicker\": s 0.65 · Easy · touches hand/kick · home walk/dash · up to 2 touches\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 18/thigh 46/rush 27; kick: ankle 16/thigh 19/rush 4 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 18/thigh 31/block 23/rush 13; dash: ankle 28/thigh 15/block 44/rush 10 | his touch lands 86% if untackled | Hold (step back) vs a real Kick: it finds nobody 65% of the time\nGOAL: stop 2 raids | FAIL: opp scores > 4 | STARS: Win within his first 3 raids; Concede at most 3\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 28/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 83/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Twist on the kick: now THEIR raider touches once and then Backward-Kicks the defender who chases him — his telegraph shows KICK before he turns, so you always see it coming. Chasing a kick is the trap (no hold catches it well, a Rush almost never). The counter is to step back: if nobody steps in (Hold), his kick finds nobody to tag 65% of the time, and his way home is still yours to Block. When he shows a Hand, Thigh Hold the touch as usual. The cost of the step-back: Hold never stops him on the touch, so the stop must come on his way home. Aha: never chase a kicker — step back, then beat his way home. Stop 2 of 5, concede no more than 4.","mechanics":["CPU backward kick","defender rush","thigh hold","ankle hold","block (defensive wall)"],"optimal":4,"branching":16,"trap":0,"explored":2157},{"n":30,"grid":"[Match · combine · Ch3 State League] OPP MAT: R T R B R T R · grip 0.80 · KEY: R rusher (touch/hop risky, Kick safe), T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), B blocker (Dash risky) · SCOUTED: a move from your last raid is tagged on its gem and ~6 pts more likely held (capped, same on every mat)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: alternate: 4 raids / 4 defences\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nCPU RAIDER \"State raider\": s 0.56 · Easy · touches hand/bonus · home dash · up to 1 touch\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1R:h38/t24/k8 2T:h50/t26 3R:h41/t27/k12 4B:h30/t27 5R:h41/t27/k12 6T:h50/t26 7R:h38/t24/k8 bonus:73 | home after 1 touch: walk 55%, dash 43%, dubki 31% | after 2: walk 66%, dash 53%, dubki 40% | if held: pull 40%, lunge 39%\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 19/thigh 49/rush 29; bonus: ankle 31/thigh 21/rush 54 | vs his way home — dash: ankle 31/thigh 17/block 48/rush 11 | his touch lands 84% if untackled\nGOAL: win by 2+ | STARS: Win by 4; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 34/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 66/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Combine chapter 3: a mat of Rushers around a Blocker and two T's, and a raider with one plan — Hand Touch or bonus hop, then always the Dash. On your raids the rushers want the Kick and the wall wants the Dubki; on his, Rush the hop and Block the Dash. 4 raids each, win by 2.","mechanics":["defence reads repeats","backward kick","rusher defenders","blocker wall","dubki","defender rush","block (defensive wall)","bonus line"],"optimal":null,"branching":22,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":31,"grid":"[Revival Run · spike · Ch3 State League] OPP MAT: o T R o B T o · grip 0.95 · KEY: o rookie, T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), R rusher (touch/hop risky, Kick safe), B blocker (Dash risky) · SCOUTED: a move from your last raid is tagged on its gem and ~6 pts more likely held (capped, same on every mat)\nMY SIDE: - - o - o - o (3 on mat)\nFLOW: alternate raids 15:00→20:00 (~7 raids in all, ~4 each) · start score 5-9\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nCPU RAIDER \"State raider\": s 0.68 · Easy · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash · up to 1 touch\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1o:h29/t10 2T:h51/t22 3R:h45/t30/k12 4o:h25/t23 5B:h34/t15 6T:h46/t15 7o:h29/t10 bonus:31 | home after 1 touch: walk 53%, dash 48%, dubki 24% | after 2: walk 64%, dash 58%, dubki 31% | if held: pull 38%, lunge 38%\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 17/thigh 45/rush 26; toe: ankle 46/thigh 16/rush 28 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 17/thigh 29/block 22/rush 13; dash: ankle 27/thigh 14/block 42/rush 9 | his touch lands 87% if untackled\nGOAL: finish within 2 | FAIL: trail by > 8 | STARS: Draw level; Land a Super Tackle\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 35/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 73/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Spike: all out at minute 5 — 5-9 down and only 3 back on the mat. Revival from trial 19 now runs a whole comeback: each point you score revives a team-mate (first out, first back), and with 3 or fewer every tackle is a Super Tackle. Aha: sacrifice greed for revivals — safe single touches rebuild the side. Reach 20:00 within 2 points; trail by 9 and it's over. A Super Tackle from three is the 3-star swing.","mechanics":["revival","all-out","super tackle","backward kick","escape lunge","dubki"],"optimal":null,"branching":19,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":32,"grid":"[Ghost Duel · breather · Ch3 State League] OPP MAT: o R o T o R o · grip 0.45 · KEY: o rookie, R rusher (touch/hop risky, Kick safe), T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky) · no scouting on this trial (no SCOUTED tags)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 4x\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1o:h10/t9 2R:h16/t15/k4 3o:h21/t11 4T:h25/t7 5o:h21/t11 6R:h16/t15/k4 7o:h10/t9 bonus:26 | home after 1 touch: walk 22%, dash 10%, dubki 14% | after 2: walk 29%, dash 14%, dubki 18% | if held: pull 44%, lunge 44%\nGOAL: beat the ghost's 3 points | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Score with 2 Kicks; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 38/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 79/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Breather after the revival spike, and the chapter's Ghost Duel: your district rival Sameer raided this friendly floodlight mat (rookies, two Rushers, one Thigh-holder, bonus line open) and his recorded score is on the board. Beat it in 4 raids — no defending, the ghost replays exactly. The toy: the floodlight crowd roars for every Backward Kick on a charging Rusher. Aha: the kick you learnt in this chapter is the safe point — Kick the R's, Toe the T, hop the bonus while all seven stand.","mechanics":["ghost duel","backward kick","rusher defenders","bonus line","toe touch"],"optimal":null,"branching":20,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":33,"grid":"[Full Match · boss · Ch3 State League] OPP MAT: R T B o B T R · grip 1.26 · KEY: R rusher (touch/hop risky, Kick safe), T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), B blocker (Dash risky), o rookie · no scouting on this trial (no SCOUTED tags)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: alternate raids 29:10→40:00 (~15 raids in all, ~8 each) · start score 11-12\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nCPU RAIDER \"State champion\": s 0.68 · Medium · touches hand/toe/bonus/kick · home walk/dash/dubki · up to 2 touches\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1R:h53/t35/k12 2T:h62/t30 3B:h42/t20 4o:h22/t19 5B:h42/t20 6T:h62/t30 7R:h53/t35/k12 bonus:75 | home after 1 touch: walk 70%, dash 74%, dubki 36% | after 2: walk 80%, dash 84%, dubki 46% | if held: pull 35%, lunge 34%\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 17/thigh 45/rush 26; toe: ankle 46/thigh 16/rush 28; bonus: ankle 28/thigh 19/rush 48; kick: ankle 15/thigh 19/rush 4 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 17/thigh 29/block 22/rush 13; dash: ankle 27/thigh 14/block 42/rush 9; dubki: ankle 30/thigh 5/block 7/rush 13 | his touch lands 87% if untackled | Hold (step back) vs a real Kick: it finds nobody 65% of the time\nGOAL: win by 1+ | STARS: Win by 3; Win by 6\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 34/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 63/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Chapter boss with a comeback, kept to one session: the last 11 minutes of the State Final (~15 raids), 11-12 down, no scouting. Full mat of Rushers, Blockers and T's; a raider who kicks chasers (step back) and hops the bonus (Rush the hop). Aha: one point back is a clean raid plus one stop — kick the rushers, Dubki the wall, and never chase his kick. Win the match.","mechanics":["full match","comeback","revival","super tackle","backward kick","escape lunge","defender rush","rusher defenders"],"optimal":null,"branching":20,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":34,"grid":"[Auction · teach · Ch4 Auction Hall] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 0.50 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: auction only\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nON SCREEN: purse helper (still needed + cheapest squad left)\nAUCTION (purse 85): Raider R8 open 35 market 45-60; Raider R6 open 12 market 14-22; Corner(ankle corner) open 12 market 14-24; Corner(thigh corner) open 10 market 12-20; Anchor(anchor) open 18 market 20-32; Anchor(anchor) open 14 market 16-26\nGOAL: buy Raider + Corner + Anchor | STARS: Keep 15 lakh in the purse; Keep 25 lakh in the purse\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 37/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 75/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Teach the auction: 6 lots — a star Raider and a cheap one, two Corners, two Anchors — and an 85-lakh purse against AI franchises. The star goes for 45-60, so buying him leaves barely enough for a Corner and an Anchor and nothing for the stars; the budget Raider, a Corner and an Anchor cost about 55. The purse helper on screen shows what is still needed and the cheapest squad left. Aha: price the whole squad, not the lot — a lot you pass on has a cheaper twin later. Buy a Raider, a Corner and an Anchor.","mechanics":["auction","player roles","purse"],"optimal":9,"branching":2,"trap":0,"explored":5400},{"n":35,"grid":"[Defend Stand · teach · Ch4 Auction Hall] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: A o o o o o T (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 5 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nCPU RAIDER \"League raider\": s 0.45 · Easy · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash · up to 1 touch\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 21/thigh 54/rush 32; toe: ankle 56/thigh 20/rush 34 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 23/thigh 39/block 29/rush 17; dash: ankle 36/thigh 19/block 55/rush 12 | his touch lands 81% if untackled\nGOAL: stop 3 raids | FAIL: opp scores > 5 | STARS: Win within his first 4 raids; Concede at most 2\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 31/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 76/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Teach specialists: your left corner is an Ankle specialist (A, ankle ×1.25), your right corner a Thigh specialist (T, thigh ×1.25). The raider attacks anywhere with Hand or Toe. Aha: switch to the specialist whose hold matches his move when he is in range. Stop 3 of 5.","mechanics":["hold specialists","ankle hold","thigh hold","cover position","defender select"],"optimal":null,"branching":13,"trap":0,"explored":40000},{"n":36,"grid":"[Defend Stand · teach · Ch4 Auction Hall] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: A o o K o o T (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 5 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nCPU RAIDER \"League raider\": s 0.36 · Easy · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash/dubki · up to 1 touch\nON SCREEN: Anchor range ring (±1 slot)\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 22/thigh 58/rush 34; toe: ankle 59/thigh 21/rush 36 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 25/thigh 43/block 31/rush 18; dash: ankle 39/thigh 21/block 59/rush 14; dubki: ankle 44/thigh 7/block 10/rush 18 | his touch lands 79% if untackled\nGOAL: stop 3 raids | FAIL: opp scores > 5 | STARS: Win within his first 4 raids; Concede at most 2\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 37/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 89/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Teach the Anchor, with his range drawn on the mat: K in slot 4 multiplies every hold by 1.15 and his tackles rarely slip, and the shaded ring shows his range — slots 3-5, the target and one either side. Inside the ring the Anchor is the tackler whatever the move; outside it he is too far (half strength), so at the corners use the corner specialist when his hold matches the move, the defender beside the target when it does not. Aha: the specialists need the right read, the Anchor only needs the raider inside his ring. Stop 3 of 5.","mechanics":["anchor","hold specialists","ankle hold","thigh hold","block (defensive wall)"],"optimal":null,"branching":13,"trap":0,"explored":40000},{"n":37,"grid":"[Defend Stand · twist · Ch4 Auction Hall] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: A o o K o o T (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 5 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nCPU RAIDER \"Feinting raider\": s 0.65 · Easy · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash/dubki · up to 1 touch · feints 30% · TELL on 60% of feints (telegraph flickers → it is a lie; a clean telegraph is true 85%)\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 18/thigh 46/rush 27; toe: ankle 47/thigh 17/rush 29 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 17/thigh 31/block 23/rush 13; dash: ankle 28/thigh 15/block 43/rush 10; dubki: ankle 31/thigh 5/block 8/rush 13 | his touch lands 86% if untackled\nGOAL: stop 2 raids | FAIL: opp scores > 5 | STARS: Win within his first 3 raids; Concede at most 3\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 37/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 88/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Twist: this raider feints — 3 raids in 10 the telegraphed move is not the real one — but feints have a tell: on 6 of 10 feints his hips turn first and the telegraph flickers (FEINT? on screen), so a flickering telegraph is a lie and a clean one is true about 85% of the time. Aha: trust a clean telegraph and counter it; against a flicker, use the all-round Anchor or an Ankle on his way home (it covers Dash and Dubki). Stop 2 of 5, concede no more than 5.","mechanics":["feints","anchor","hold specialists","block (defensive wall)","ankle hold","thigh hold"],"optimal":4,"branching":16,"trap":0,"explored":1537},{"n":38,"grid":"[Match · practise · Ch4 Auction Hall] OPP MAT: A T B o B T A · grip 0.98 · KEY: A ankle-catcher (Toe/hop/Dubki risky), T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), B blocker (Dash risky), o rookie · SCOUTED: a move from your last raid is tagged on its gem and ~6 pts more likely held (capped, same on every mat)\nMY SIDE: A T o K o T A (7 on mat)\nFLOW: alternate: 4 raids / 4 defences · start score 20-19\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nCPU RAIDER \"League captain\": s 0.58 · Hard · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash · up to 1 touch\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1A:h29/t44 2T:h47/t33 3B:h35/t16 4o:h18/t15 5B:h35/t16 6T:h47/t33 7A:h29/t44 bonus:54 | home after 1 touch: walk 58%, dash 66%, dubki 55% | after 2: walk 69%, dash 77%, dubki 66% | if held: pull 38%, lunge 37%\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 19/thigh 49/rush 28; toe: ankle 50/thigh 18/rush 30 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 19/thigh 33/block 25/rush 14; dash: ankle 31/thigh 16/block 47/rush 11 | his touch lands 85% if untackled\nGOAL: win by 1+ | FAIL: trail by > 1 | STARS: Win by 3; No empty raids\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 34/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 67/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Game management against a strong captain: you lead 20-19 with 4 raids each to go, and the trial is lost the moment you trail by more than 1. Your specialist squad defends (A corners, T covers, Anchor in the middle) against a Hard-thinking league captain who counters your specialists. A patient empty raid is safe while you lead, but two in a row make the third a Do-or-Die. Aha: protecting a lead is its own skill — bank the safe single touch, spend at most one empty raid, and tackle only with the specialist whose hold matches his move. Finish ahead, never more than 1 behind.","mechanics":["game management","empty-raid counter","hold specialists","anchor","alternating raids"],"optimal":null,"branching":10,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":39,"grid":"[Defend Stand · twist · Ch4 Auction Hall] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: A o T K T o A (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 4 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nCPU RAIDER \"Two-touch raider\": s 0.64 · Medium · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash · up to 