h in the purse\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 40/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 69/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Combine auction and defence: the scouting report says their raider is a Toe-Touch specialist who Dubkis home — both beaten by Ankle holds. The Ankle Corner is the one you want, so the rival franchises bid him up; the Thigh Corner goes cheap and the Anchor sits between. 74 lakh buys the Ankle Corner and an Anchor only if you don't overpay. Aha: buy for the opponent you will face, not the bargain. Buy a Corner and an Anchor, then stop 2 of his 5 raids.","mechanics":["auction","hold specialists","anchor","ankle hold","thigh hold","scouting"],"optimal":11,"branching":2,"trap":null,"explored":36578},{"n":42,"grid":"[Auction · twist · Ch4 Auction Hall] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 0.90 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: auction only\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nON SCREEN: purse helper (still needed + cheapest squad left)\nAUCTION (purse 75): Anchor(anchor) open 18 market 34-48; Raider R8 open 25 market 28-46; Corner(ankle corner) open 12 market 14-26; Raider R5 open 12 market 12-24; Anchor(anchor) open 15 market 18-30\nRIVAL BIDDER: Harbour Hawks chase the FIRST Anchor (+14 lakh on his value), then stop\nGOAL: buy Raider + Anchor | STARS: Keep 10 lakh in the purse; Keep 18 lakh in the purse\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 39/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 67/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touc