d the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Twist, auction only — read the other bidder: the Harbour Hawks need an Anchor and chase the FIRST one on the list, paying about 14 lakh over his market value (shown in the lot's market range); once they have one they stop. You need a Raider and an Anchor from 75 lakh, and the purse helper shows the sum on every bid. Aha: let the rival overpay for the first Anchor — his twin later goes at market, and that saving buys the better Raider.","mechanics":["auction","rival bidder","player roles","anchor","purse"],"optimal":9,"branching":2,"trap":0,"explored":4894},{"n":43,"grid":"[Super Challenge · breather · Ch4 Auction Hall] OPP MAT: R o R o R o o · grip 0.38 · KEY: R rusher (touch/hop risky, Kick safe), o rookie · no scouting on this trial (no SCOUTED tags)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat) · raider reach 7 agi 6 spd 6\nFLOW: you raid 4x\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1R:h12/t11/k2 2o:h13/t12 3R:h13/t12/k3 4o:h13/t12 5R:h13/t12/k3 6o:h9/t9 7o:h4/t4 bonus:34 | home after 1 touch: walk 14%, dash 7%, dubki 13% | after 2: walk 19%, dash 9%, dubki 17% | if held: pull 52%, lunge 50%\nGOAL: score 4, 2x kick | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Land a bonus hop; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 36/40 (best 2★), a mid-skill player 83/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Breather with a toy: the fans' trick-shot exhibition. Three Rushers charge on a friendly mat and the crowd wants Backward Kicks — score 2 Kicks on the way to 4 points in 4 raids (a bonus hop first is the show-off star), with your squad's raider (reach 7). Aha: an exhibition is the place to try the show moves you will need later — kick the charge, hop the line while seven stand.","mechanics":["backward kick","rusher defenders","bonus line","score attack"],"optimal":null,"branching":21,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":44,"grid":"[Full Match · boss · Ch4 Auction Hall] OPP MAT: A T R B R T A · grip 1.31 · KEY: A ankle-catcher (Toe/hop/Dubki risky), T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), R rusher (touch/hop risky, Kick safe), B blocker (Dash risky) · SCOUTED: a move from your last raid is tagged on its gem and ~6 pts more likely held (capped, same on every mat)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat) · raider reach 7 agi 6 spd 6\nFLOW: alternate raids 00:00→10:00 (~14 raids in all, ~7 each, half-time swap at 05:00)\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nCPU RAIDER \"Franchise captain\": s 0.69 · Medium · touches hand/toe/bonus · home walk/dash/dubki · up to 2 touches · feints 15%\nAUCTION (purse 75): Raider R8 open 25 market 30-55; Corner(ankle corner) open 12 market 14-28; Anchor(anchor) open 18 market 20-36; Cover(cover) open 10 market 12-22; Corner(thigh corner) open 10 market 12-24; Anchor(anchor) open 15 market 16-30; Cover(cover) open 8 market 8-18\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1A:h35/t52 2T:h60/t46 3R:h55/t38/k17 4B:h42/t39 5R:h55/t38/k17 6T:h60/t46 7A:h35/t52 bonus:81 | home after 1 touch: walk 70%, dash 59%, dubki 69% | after 2: walk 80%, dash 70%, dubki 79% | if held: pull 39%, lunge 36%\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 17/thigh 44/rush 26; toe: ankle 45/thigh 16/rush 27; bonus: ankle 27/thigh 18/rush 48 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 16/thigh 29/block 21/rush 12; dash: ankle 26/thigh 14/block 41/rush 9; dubki: ankle 30/thigh 5/block 7/rush 12 | his touch lands 87% if untackled\nGOAL: win by 1+ | STARS: Win by 4; Win by 7\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 29/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 61/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, l