played exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Chapter boss: the Season Final as a 2x5 mini-Blitz (~14 raids), with an OPTIONAL pre-match auction — 75 lakh, 7 lots (two Corners, two Covers, two Anchors, one star Raider); buy who you like or nobody, every buy strengthens the squad that plays. Then a Medium franchise that reads your specialists and feints 15%. Aha: the auction is preparation, not a gate — three mid-price defenders cover more slots than one star. Win the match.","mechanics":["full match","optional auction","player roles","hold specialists","anchor","cover","feints","defender switch"],"optimal":null,"branching":2,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":45,"grid":"[Super Challenge · teach · Ch5 Continental Cup] OPP MAT: o o o o o T o · grip 0.99 · KEY: o rookie, T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky) · no scouting on this trial (no SCOUTED tags)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 4x\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1o:h11/t10 2o:h15/t13 3o:h15/t13 4o:h15/t13 5o:h32/t13 6T:h47/t14 7o:h30/t10 bonus:11 | home after 1 touch: walk 34%, dash 20%, dubki 19% | after 2: walk 43%, dash 27%, dubki 25% | if held: pull 38%, lunge 37%\nGOAL: 1x superRaid | FAIL: raider out 3x | STARS: Never get caught; Super Raid within 2 raids\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 38/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 71/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Teach the Super Raid on a soft mat: six rookies and one Thigh-holder on the right. Three touches in one raid take 21 of the 30 seconds and every touch makes the way home harder (depth ×1.7 at three, READ: home after 1 vs after 2), so the route matters: three rookies in a row on the LEFT, away from the T, then Dubki home. No scouting in this lesson. Aha: string the touches along the soft side, then duck home before the clock. Land a Super Raid within 4 raids — the spare raid lets you learn the route.","mechanics":["super raid","raid clock","hand touch","toe touch","dubki"],"optimal":null,"branching":18,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":46,"grid":"[Defend Stand · teach · Ch5 Continental Cup] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 4 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush chain hold\nCPU RAIDER \"Continental raider\": s 0.49 · Easy · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash · up to 1 touch\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 20/thigh 52/rush 30/chain 49; toe: ankle 54/thigh 19/rush 33/chain 45 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 21/thigh 37/block 27/rush 16/chain 50; dash: ankle 34/thigh 18/block 52/rush 12/chain 43 | his touch lands 82% if untackled\nGOAL: 1x chain | FAIL: opp scores > 2 | STARS: Chain him within his first 2 raids; Concede at most 1\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 36/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 83/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Teach the Chain Tackle: two adjacent defenders link. It is the one tackle with no wrong read — about as strong as the RIGHT hold on any touch (READ: chain ~45-49 vs the matching hold ~52-54, while the wrong hold is ~20), and the best stop of all on his walk home — but a broken chain costs two men, and the Dubki ducks under it. Aha: two defenders, one chain — when you are unsure of his move, chain the pair around his target; when you are sure, the matching hold is as good and risks one man. Land a chain tackle in his 4 raids and concede no more than 2 — one clean chain is the lesson, and a wrong pair costs a point.","mechanics":["chain tackle","ankle hold","thigh hold","block (defensive wall)","defender rush"],"optimal":2,"branching":18,"trap":0,"explored":63},{"n":47,"grid":"[Super Challenge · twist · Ch5 Continental Cup] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: - - o o o - - (3 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 4 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush chain hold\nCPU RAIDER \"Super raider\": s 0.69 · Easy · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash/dubki · up to 2 touches\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 17/thigh 44/rush 26/chain 42; toe: ankle 45/thigh 16/rush 27/chain 39 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 16/thigh 29/block 21/rush 12/chain 40; dash: ankle 26/thigh 14/block 41/rush 9/chain 35; dubki: ankle 30/thigh 5/block 7/rush 12/chain 11 | his touch lands 87% if untackled\nGOAL: 1x superTackle | FAIL: opp scores > 2 | STARS: Super Tackle with a chain; Concede nothing\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 38/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 85/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Twist: three rookies left in the middle of your mat, no specialists, against a raider who goes for two touches. Any tackle from 3 is a Super Tackle (+2), but a failed tackle on the touch costs two men and brings the all-out close. Aha: let the first touch go and chain him on the way home, when every tackle still counts as Super — unless his telegraph shows the Dubki, which ducks under any chain (Ankle him instead). Land a Super Tackle within his 4 raids, concede no more than 2 — one bad read is survivable, two are not.","mechanics":["chain tackle","super tackle","super raid","all-out"],"optimal":2,"branching":11,"trap":0,"explored":40},{"n":48,"grid":"[Raid Puzzle · teach · Ch5 Formation: Cage] OPP MAT: o C C o C C o · grip 1.02 · KEY: o rookie, C chain link (walk/Dash risky when paired) · SCOUTED: a move from your last raid is tagged on its gem and ~7 pts more likely held (capped, same on every mat)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 5x\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1o:h15/t13 2C:h25/t22 3C:h25/t22 4o:h22/t19 5C:h25/t22 6C:h25/t22 7o:h15/t13 bonus:12 | home after 1 touch: walk 60%, dash 62%, dubki 19% | after 2: walk 71%, dash 73%, dubki 25% | if held: pull 27%, lunge 27%\nGOAL: score 4 | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Win within 4 raids; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 34/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 72/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Teach formation themes with the Cage: two chained pairs (C C) either side of the centre. Walking or dashing home past two chains is held most of the time; the Dubki ducks under both (READ). Aha: in the Cage, the way home is the puzzle. Score 4 in 5 raids — one spare raid to learn the Cage.","mechanics":["formation theme: Cage","chain links","dubki","toe touch","hand touch"],"optimal":null,"branching":18,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":49,"grid":"[Raid Puzzle · twist · Ch5 Formation: Pincer] OPP MAT: T R o B o R T · grip 0.19 · KEY: T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), R rusher (touch/hop risky, Kick safe), o rookie, B blocker (Dash risky) · no scouting on this trial (no SCOUTED tags)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 5x\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1T:h13/t4 2R:h12/t7/k3 3o:h6/t5 4B:h4/t3 5o:h6/t5 6R:h12/t7/k3 7T:h13/t4 bonus:14 | home after 1 touch: walk 15%, dash 13%, dubki 7% | after 2: walk 20%, dash 17%, dubki 9% | if held: pull 47%, lunge 47%\nGOAL: score 3, 1x bonus | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Score with a Kick; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 37/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 68/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Twist theme, the Pincer: Thigh-holder corners and two Rushers just inside them squeeze the bonus line. The goal has one must: a bonus point among your 3 points in 5 raids. The hop is the riskiest option on this mat (READ bonus), but a failed hop just ends the raid — and every touch you make before it puts a man out, so below six standing the bonus line is dead (the Bonus gem disappears). No scouting here. The Kick on a charging R is the safest point on the mat, the Toe beats the T's. Aha: hop first, while all seven stand — then kick the rushers for the rest.","mechanics":["formation theme: Pincer","thigh-holders","rusher defenders","bonus line","backward kick"],"optimal":null,"branching":20,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":50,"grid":"[Raid Puzzle · teach · Ch5 Continental Cup] OPP MAT: o o T o T o o · grip 1.05 · KEY: o rookie, T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky) · SCOUTED: a move from your last raid is tagged on its gem and ~7 pts more likely held (capped, same on every mat)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 4x · DRS reviews 1\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1o:h12/t10 2o:h34/t14 3T:h48/t15 4o:h48/t15 5T:h48/t15 6o:h34/t14 7o:h12/t10 bonus:12 | home after 1 touch: walk 48%, dash 26%, dubki 21% | after 2: walk 59%, dash 33%, dubki 27% | if held: pull 37%, lunge 36%\nGOAL: score 4 | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Win a DRS review; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 35/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 70/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Teach DRS on an easy mat, so the review is the only lesson: rookies with two Thigh-holders. Close touches are called by the referee and the call says how close: 'very tight' calls are wrong almost half the time, 'tight' ones 1 in 5 — and until you use your first review every close call here comes up 'very tight' and wrong, so the lesson always comes up. You have 1 review and a failed review is lost. Aha: spend the one review on a very tight call, accept the merely tight ones — a review is a resource, not a reflex. Score 4 in 4 raids — one point a raid, so a wrong call you don't review costs the trial.","mechanics":["DRS review","toe touch","hand touch","dubki"],"optimal":null,"branching":18,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":51,"grid":"[Ghost Duel · twist · Ch5 Formation: Ghost Gate] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 5 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush chain hold\nCPU RAIDER \"Ghost raider\": s 0.67 · Easy · touches hand/toe/bonus · home walk/dash/dubki · up to 1 touch · GHOST PLAN: toe@1>dash | hand@3>walk | bonus>walk | hand@5,toe@4>dubki | toe@0>dash\nON SCREEN: the ghost's next raid plan shown above the mat; the matching counter stops +15 pts (in the READ row)\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 17/thigh 56/rush 26/chain 43; toe: ankle 58/thigh 16/rush 28/chain 40; bonus: ankle 28/thigh 19/rush 60/chain 25 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 17/thigh 41/block 22/rush 13/chain 54; dash: ankle 27/thigh 14/block 55/rush 9/chain 36; dubki: ankle 42/thigh 5/block 7/rush 13/chain 11 | his touch lands 87% if untackled\nGOAL: stop 3 raids | FAIL: opp scores > 3 | STARS: Win within his first 4 raids; Land a chain tackle\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 27/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 70/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Twist: defend against a recorded ghost raider. Its 5 raids are known before you start (GHOST PLAN row: a Toe and Dash home, a Hand and walk, a bonus hop, a two-touch raid with a Dubki home, a corner Toe and Dash) and replay exactly — no feints — so the right counter is set up in advance and stops about 15 points more than usual (READ: Thigh v Hand, Ankle v Toe and Dubki, Rush v the hop, Block v the Dash, Chain v the walk). A chain tackle is the 3-star show but it costs two men if it breaks. Aha: a ghost can be solved: plan the perfect counter for each raid. Stop 3 of 5 and concede no more than 3.","mechanics":["ghost gate","chain tackle","block (defensive wall)","ankle hold","thigh hold","defender rush"],"optimal":null,"branching":15,"trap":0,"explored":40000},{"n":52,"grid":"[Match · combine · Ch5 Formation: Diamond] OPP MAT: o T R B R T o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie, T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), R rusher (touch/hop risky, Kick safe), B blocker (Dash risky) · SCOUTED: a move from your last raid is tagged on its gem and ~7 pts more likely held (capped, same on every mat)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: alternate: 4 raids / 4 defences\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush chain hold\nCPU RAIDER \"Continental raider\": s 0.62 · Medium · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash · up to 2 touches\nON SCREEN: Blocker wall drawn on the midline; the Dash gem carries a WALLED tag with its real % (shown, never a hidden trap)\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1o:h30/t10 2T:h53/t23 3R:h48/t32/k14 4B:h36/t33 5R:h48/t32/k14 6T:h53/t23 7o:h30/t10 bonus:49 | home after 1 touch: walk 58%, dash 50%, dubki 30% | after 2: walk 69%, dash 61%, dubki 38% | if held: pull 38%, lunge 37%\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 18/thigh 47/rush 27/chain 45; toe: ankle 48/thigh 17/rush 29/chain 41 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 18/thigh 32/block 24/rush 14/chain 44; dash: ankle 29/thigh 16/block 45/rush 10/chain 38 | his touch lands 85% if untackled\nGOAL: win by 2+ | STARS: Win by 4; Land a chain tackle\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 36/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 70/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed