 3o:h13/t12 4C:h12/t10 5C:h12/t10 6o:h9/t8 7o:h5/t5 bonus:16 | home after 1 touch: walk 24%, dash 23%, dubki 11% | after 2: walk 31%, dash 29%, dubki 15% | if held: pull 40%, lunge 39%\nGOAL: beat the ghost's 4 points | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Land a bonus hop; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 36/40 (best 2★), a mid-skill player 82/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Breather after the ghost spike, and a new toy: Arun — your friend's ghost from trial 21 — wants a rematch on the continental fan-zone mat, and he has learnt the chapter: one chained pair in the middle, a Rusher on the left, rookies elsewhere, bonus line open. Beat his recorded score in 4 raids, no defending. Aha: a friendly mat still has one trap — never walk or Dash past the chained pair; hop the bonus while seven stand, kick the Rusher, and Dubki home whenever the chain is up.","mechanics":["ghost duel","chain links","dubki","bonus line","backward kick"],"optimal":null,"branching":19,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":55,"grid":"[Full Match · boss · Ch5 Continental Cup] OPP MAT: o C C o C C o · grip 1.46 · KEY: o rookie, C chain link (walk/Dash risky when paired) · SCOUTED: a move from your last raid is tagged on its gem and ~7 pts more likely held (capped, same on every mat)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat) · raider reach 7 agi 6 spd 6\nFLOW: alternate raids 05:40→14:20 (~12 raids in all, ~6 each, half-time swap at 10:00) · start score 5-6\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush chain hold\nCPU RAIDER \"Continental captain\": s 0.68 · Medium · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash/dubki · up to 2 touches\nMOMENT (reversal, at half-time): \"HALF-TIME REVERSAL! They drop the Cage for 