onship] OPP MAT: o T o o o T o · grip 1.29 · KEY: o rookie, T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky) · no scouting on this trial (no SCOUTED tags)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat) · raiders Veer R8 A7 S7 st2, Kabir R5 A6 S5 st8 (fatigue)\nFLOW: alternate: 5 raids / 5 defences\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush chain hold\nCPU RAIDER \"World raider\": s 0.54 · Easy · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash · up to 1 touch\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1o:h34/t12 2T:h52/t16 3o:h37/t16 4o:h17/t15 5o:h37/t16 6T:h52/t16 7o:h34/t12 bonus:13 | home after 1 touch: walk 54%, dash 28%, dubki 23% | after 2: walk 65%, dash 36%, dubki 29% | if held: pull 49%, lunge 40%\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 19/thigh 50/rush 29/chain 47; toe: ankle 51/thigh 18/rush 31/chain 43 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 20/thigh 35/block 26/rush 15/chain 48; dash: ankle 32/thigh 17/block 49/rush 11/chain 41 | his touch lands 84% if untackled\nGOAL: win by 4+ | STARS: Win by 6; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 34/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 73/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting'