"n":57,"grid":"[Raid Puzzle · teach · Ch6 World Championship] OPP MAT: - T A K A T - (captain weak to kick) · grip 0.66 · KEY: T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), A ankle-catcher (Toe/hop/Dubki risky), K captain · no scouting on this trial (no SCOUTED tags)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 5x\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 2T:h32/t21 3A:h31/t41 4K:h28/t47/k9 5A:h31/t41 6T:h32/t21 | home after 1 touch: walk 46%, dash 30%, dubki 49% | after 2: walk 57%, dash 39%, dubki 60% | if held: pull 36%, lunge 36%\nGOAL: score 4 | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Score with a kick on the captain; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 34/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 67/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Teach rival captains: five on their mat (so the bonus line is dead) and their captain K anchors the centre — every move near him is dangerous and he guards every way home. His one weakness: he chases, so a Backward Kick on him is the safest touch on the mat (READ k on slot 4), and the kick tags him out of the way home too. No scouting in this lesson. Aha: kick the captain, don't avoid him. Score 4 in 5 raids.","mechanics":["rival captain","backward kick","ankle-catchers","thigh-holders","dubki"],"optimal":null,"branching":14,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":58,"grid":"[Defend Stand · teach · Ch6 World Championship] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 6 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush chain hold\nCPU RAIDER \"The Dubki King\": s 0.54 · Medium · touches hand/kick · home dubki · up to 1 touch\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 20/thigh 50/rush 29/chain 47; kick: ankle 17/thigh 21/rush 4/chain 36 | vs his way home — dubki: ankle 36/thigh 6/block 9/rush 15/chain 13 | his touch lands 83% if untackled | Hold (step back) vs a real Kick: it finds nobody 65% of the time\nGOAL: stop 3 raids | FAIL: opp scores > 4 | STARS: Win within his first 4 raids; Concede at most 1\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 29/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 73/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Rival raider: the Dubki King always ducks home — under thighs, chains and walls — and only the Ankle Hold reads the dubki (READ). He knows you know: his touch is a Hand or a Backward Kick at whoever chases him, so the touch is a second read — Thigh the Hand, step back (Stay Back) from the Kick. Aha: a signature move is a promise — never chase the touch you can't win, and ankle him on the way home. Stop 3 of 6 and concede no more than 4.","mechanics":["rival raider signature","ankle hold","chain tackle","CPU backward kick","step back vs a kick"],"optimal":null,"branching":15,"trap":0,"explored":40000},{"n":59,"grid":"[Defend Stand · twist · Ch6 World Championship] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o C K C o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 4 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush chain hold\nCPU RAIDER \"The Feint Master\": s 0.57 · Medium · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash/dubki · up to 1 touch · feints 15% · TELL on 75% of feints (telegraph flickers → it is a lie; a clean telegraph is true 96%)\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 19/thigh 49/rush 29/chain 56; toe: ankle 50/thigh 18/rush 31/chain 52 | vs his way home — w