 rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Twist on rival raiders: the Feint Master feints about 1 raid in 7 and, like every feinter since trial 37, has a tell: on 3 of 4 feints his hips turn before the shown move and the telegraph flickers (FEINT? on screen) — then the shown move is a lie. With no tell, the telegraph is true about 24 times in 25. Your Anchor stands between two Covers, so a chain through the centre is strong whichever touch is real, and the Ankle covers both his Dash and his Dubki home. Aha: read the tell — trust a clean telegraph, and against a flicker use the move that has no weakness. Stop 2 of his 4 raids, concede no more than 2.","mechanics":["feints","feint tell","rival raider signature","chain tackle","anchor","ankle hold"],"optimal":4,"branching":15,"trap":0,"explored":1164},{"n":60,"grid":"[Match · combine · Ch6 World Championship] OPP MAT: R T o K o T R (captain weak to toe) · grip 1.26 · KEY: R rusher (touch/hop risky, Kick safe), T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), o rookie, K captain · SCOUTED: a move from your last raid is tagged on its gem and ~7 pts more likely held (capped, same on every mat)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat) · raiders Veer R8 A7 S7 st3, Kabir R6 A6 S5 st8, Dev R6 A7 S6 st6 (fatigue)\nFLOW: alternate raids 30:00→40:00 (~14 raids in all, ~7 each) · start score 16-18\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | 