 at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Combine fatigue with a reversal: the last 10 minutes of a group match (~14 raids), 16-18 down, with three raiders to rotate (one star, two workhorses) against a mat anchored by a rival captain weak to the Toe Touch, with rookies either side of him so his Toe gem is the safest on the mat. After 6 raids their captain tires and goes to the bench: a fresh Rusher takes the centre, so the captain's Toe weakness is gone and the Kick on the charging R becomes the centre's safe touch. Aha: rest the star for the raids after the swap, and re-read the centre when the captain leaves. Win by 1.","mechanics":["defence reads repeats","fatigue","raider rotation","rival captain","backward kick","chain tackle","dubki","mid-match reversal"],"optimal":null,"branching":3,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":61,"grid":"[Raid Puzzle · combine · Ch6 Formation: Cage] OPP MAT: o C C K T T o (captain weak to dash) · grip 0.85 · KEY: o rookie, C chain link (walk/Dash risky when paired), K captain, T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky) · SCOUTED: a move from your last raid is tagged on its gem and ~9 pts more likely held (capped, same on every mat)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 6x\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1o:h13/t11 2C:h21/t19 3C:h32/t30 4K:h48/t36/k38 5T:h59/t24 6T:h52/t12 7o:h26/t9 bonus:10 | home after 1 touch: walk 66%, dash 44%, dubki 35% | after 2: walk 76%, dash 55%, dubki 44% | if held: pull 33%, lunge 32%\nGOAL: score 4 | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Land a Super Raid; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 31/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 65/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Combine: a half-Cage with a rival captain at its hinge — a chained pair on the left, the captain in the centre, two T's on the right. Two ways home compete (READ): the Dubki ducks under the chain and the T's but not the captain; the Dash is the captain's weakness (he cannot turn) but runs into the chain. And the answer moves: every chain link you put out breaks the chain for the next raid, so the Dash gets safer raid by raid. Aha: there is no fixed answer — re-price the way home after every raid. Score 4 in 6 raids; a Super Raid is the 3-star swing.","mechanics":["rival captain","formation theme: Cage","chain links","dubki","dash home","backward kick","super raid"],"optimal":null,"branching":19,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":62,"grid":"[Match · combine · Ch6 Formation: Wall] OPP MAT: B B o K o B B (captain weak to toe) · grip 1.06 · KEY: B blocker (Dash risky), o rookie, K captain · no scouting on this trial (no SCOUTED tags)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: alternate: 5 raids / 5 defences · start score 9-11\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush chain hold\nCPU RAIDER \"World raider\": s 0.64 · Medium · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash/dubki · up to 2 touches\nON SCREEN: Blocker wall drawn on the midline; the Dash gem carries a WALLED tag with its real % (shown, never a hidden trap)\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1B:h17/t15 2B:h21/t18 3o:h31/t14 4K:h41/t12/k41 5o:h31/t14 6B:h21/t18 7B:h17/t15 bonus:16 | home after 1 touch: walk 60%, dash 89%, dubki 44% | after 2: walk 71%, dash 95%, dubki 54% | if held: pull 28%, lunge 28%\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 18/thigh 46/rush 27/chain 44; toe: ankle 47/thigh 17/rush 29/chain 40 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 18/thigh 31/block 23/rush 13/chain 43; dash: ankle 28/thigh 15/block 44/rush 10/chain 37; dubki: ankle 32/thigh 5/block 8/rush 13/chain 12 | his touch lands 86% if untackled\nGOAL: win by 1+ | STARS: Win by 3; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 34/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 69/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Combine with the Wall theme: four Blockers link arms on the midline around a captain weak to the Toe Touch, with rookies beside him, against a Medium raider who never feints. The Dash gem is drawn WALLED — it is legal but the wall eats it (READ) — so every way home is costly here (READ after one touch: Dubki ~44%, walk ~60%, the WALLED Dash ~89%) — the Dubki is the least bad, and no scouting on this trial. That price is the puzzle: the touch is cheap (a Toe on the captain, his weakness, ~12%), the way home is not, so a second touch is almost never worth it. Aha: against a wall, one touch and Dubki — bank single points and win the match on your defence. Joined at 9-11 down, 5 raids each, win by 1.","mechanics":["formation theme: Wall","rival captain","blocker wall","defence reads repeats","chain tackle"],"optimal":null,"branching":19,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":63,"grid":"[Ghost Duel · breather · Ch6 World Championship] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.29 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o C K C o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 4 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush chain hold\nCPU RAIDER \"Legend's ghost\": s 0.44 · Easy · touches hand/toe · home walk · up to 1 touch · GHOST PLAN: hand@3>walk | toe@2>walk | hand@4>walk | toe@3>walk\nON SCREEN: the ghost's next raid plan shown above the mat; the matching counter stops +15 pts (in the READ row)\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 21/thigh 67/rush 32/chain 61; toe: ankle 68/thigh 20/rush 34/chain 56 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 23/thigh 52/block 32/rush 17/chain 78 | his touch lands 81% if untackled\nGOAL: 1x chain | FAIL: opp scores > 1 | STARS: Chain him within his first 2 raids; Concede nothing\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 38/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 77/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds. ASSISTS: 3 free coach hints per trial (best move on the real engine); after a failed attempt, Try Again opens with the coach guiding the first raid (retry assist). GHOST DUELS (async PvP, a recorded real run replayed exactly) are the breathers of chapters 2, 3, 5 and 6 (21, 32, 54, 63) plus the spike 53 and the Ghost Gate 51.","intent":"Breather with a toy before the last push: the legends' lap of honour as a Ghost Duel on defence. A retired champion's ghost replays four recorded raids — the plan is on screen above the mat (Hand and walk, Toe and walk, Hand and walk, Toe and walk), no feints — into your Anchor and two Covers; the crowd wants a Chain Tackle. Land 1 chain and concede no more than 1 (a chain inside his first 2 raids is the show-off star). The cost: a broken chain lets him tag both links, so a wild chain far from his target is worse than a plain Thigh Hold. Aha: a chain is two men, one tackle — link the pair either side of his target and let the Covers do the lifting.","mechanics":["ghost gate","chain tackle","cover","anchor","score attack"],"optimal":2,"branching":18,"trap":0,"explored":47},{"n":64,"grid":"[Revival Run · spike · Ch6 World Championship] OPP MAT: o T A K A T o (captain weak to kick) · grip 1.32 · KEY: o rookie, T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), A ankle-catcher (Toe/hop/Dubki risky), K captain · SCOUTED: a move from your last raid is tagged on its gem and ~9 pts more likely held (capped, same on every mat)\nMY SIDE: - o o K o - - (4 on mat)\nFLOW: alternate raids 33:00→40:00 (~10 raids in all, ~5 each) · start score 24-25\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush chain hold\nCPU RAIDER \"World raider\": s 0.68 · Hard · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash/dubki · up to 2 touches · feints 15%\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1o:h37/t13 2T:h56/t40 3A:h52/t65 4K:h48/t72/k18 5A:h52/t65 6T:h56/t40 7o:h37/t13 bonus:15 | home after 1 touch: walk 73%, dash 55%, dubki 76% | after 2: walk 83%, dash 66%, dubki 86% | if held: pull 23%, lunge 23%\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 17/thigh 45/rush 26/chain 48; toe: ankle 46/thigh 16/rush 28/chain 44 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 17/thigh 29/block 22/rush 13/chain 45; dash: ankle 27/thigh 14/block 42/rush 9/chain 39; dubki: ankle 30/thigh 5/block 7/rush 13/chain 12 | his touch lands 87% if untackled\nGOAL: win by 1+ | FAIL: trail by > 9 | STARS: Win by 3; Land a Super Tackle\nPROOF (v